# Review ownership.
#
# A team handle rather than an individual: this repository is an asset intended
# for sale, and ownership should survive a change of maintainer without a commit.
# No personal names appear anywhere in this repository, including here.
#
# SETUP REQUIRED: create the `maintainers` team in the owning organisation and
# grant it write access, or this file resolves to nobody and silently assigns no
# reviewer.
#
# Note: this repository is trunk-only — everything lands on main and no branch
# survives — so CODEOWNERS assigns reviewers only if pull requests are ever
# introduced. It is here so ownership is declared, not because a PR flow exists.

*                       @Airgate-Pty-Ltd/maintainers

# The decision layer. Changes here alter what the product determines, not how it
# looks — routing, dispositions, gates, and record integrity all live below.
/src/engine/            @Airgate-Pty-Ltd/maintainers
/src/documents/         @Airgate-Pty-Ltd/maintainers

# The clean-room gate and CI. A weakening change here is the one that cannot be
# undone later, because git history is permanent.
/scripts/               @Airgate-Pty-Ltd/maintainers
/.husky/                @Airgate-Pty-Ltd/maintainers
/.github/               @Airgate-Pty-Ltd/maintainers

# Regulatory content and citations.
/src/content/           @Airgate-Pty-Ltd/maintainers
/REGULATORY-SOURCES.md  @Airgate-Pty-Ltd/maintainers
/LICENSE                @Airgate-Pty-Ltd/maintainers
